#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0196 expect=violation domain=PP
#note "S3 foreign discrimination (SKELETON-distinct-function hazard 3). Authority: SEND Conformance Rules v5.0 SEND196 (Rule: PPCAT is the name of the analyte in PCTEST whose profile the parameter is associated with). Partially Executable (underreporting): the Check tests membership in the study-wide PC.PCTEST set, not the per-profile association; here every PP row names the analyte of its own subject PC profile, so the unchecked association is not violated (plan §2.4). Row 1's PPCAT METABOLITE Z is not the name of any PCTEST analyte in PC -> fires. The primary PP deliberately carries a PCTEST column (PP normally has none; the rule has no Requirements.Variables.None) holding the same METABOLITE Z: a port that read PCTEST from the primary PP instead of the FOREIGN PC would find it in its own set and fall silent."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 USUBJID=S1-002 PPCAT="METABOLITE Z"
dataset PP class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Parameters"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PPSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PPTESTCD type=Char label="Parameter Short Name"
col PPCAT    type=Char label="Parameter Category"
col PCTEST   type=Char label="Test Name"
col PPORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
S1 | PP | S1-002 | 1 | CMAX | METABOLITE Z | METABOLITE Z | 5.2
---

dataset PC class=FINDINGS label="Pharmacokinetics Concentrations"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col PCSEQ    type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col PCTESTCD type=Char label="Test Short Name"
col PCTEST   type=Char label="Test Name"
col PCORRES  type=Char label="Result or Finding in Original Units"
---
S1 | PC | S1-001 | 1 | DRUGX  | DRUG X      | 12.5
S1 | PC | S1-002 | 1 | DRUGX  | DRUG X      | 13.1
S1 | PC | S1-002 | 2 | METABY | METABOLITE Y | 2.4
---
